35,2,1,talk,Servas,,The data is clear. Broad tools fail; narrow ones survive. We must be specific.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,The capital line is frozen. But the software allowance has room. Fixed fees are stable.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh no. Half the sites have no signal, and developers are busy until Q3.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,We lose an hour daily copying records. Eleven misrouted deliveries from bad data.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,Two people do all the coordination work by hand. And clerks re-request the same certificates.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, the frozen capital is a constraint, but the recurring allowance is open.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,Yes. We can use the software allowance. Fixed-fee work is cheaper than per-head licences.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Ryuji, if we can't build it in-house, we need a vendor. But the signal is bad.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, the data errors are the real problem. We need a central source of truth.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, the coordination group is broken. We need a tool to reduce their manual load.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,A central repository for supplier records would address the data errors and reduce copying.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"That fits the budget. It is a software allowance item, not a capital one.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,But what about the field app? The signal issue is a dealbreaker for mobile sync.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,The field app is risky. The data hub is a direct fix for the daily losses I see.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,The data hub also helps the clerks stop re-requesting certificates. It solves multiple problems.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Servas,,"I agree. The pattern shows narrow, specific tools succeed. A data hub is specific.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I am comfortable with this. It uses the available budget and avoids capital freeze issues.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,"Okay. If the field app is too risky, the data hub is a solid alternative.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,It addresses the root cause of the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,It reduces the manual burden on the coordination group and the clerks. I support it.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
